cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Code Futures"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Given a repository, say what state its engineering practice is in. Code
  Futures reports on code structure — where complexity and churn concentrate,
  which files keep changing together, where a module boundary is leaking — and
  on the practice around it: linting, testing, review gates, dependency
  hygiene, and the open-source baseline. It produces a report per repository
  and a machine-readable snapshot, and knows nothing about courses, teams, or
  people. The name follows Kent Beck's distinction between features, which are
  what software does now, and futures, which are what remains possible later.
authors:
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Shown
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-5716-8835"
    affiliation: Saint Louis University
repository-code: "https://github.com/oss-slu/code-futures"
